## 1. System Overview & Macro Scale Metrics

The openOODA project implements Colonel John Boyd's Observe-Orient-Decide-Act (OODA) loop.
The system elevates the loop from a military tactic to a sovereign computational substrate.
The standard library contains zero external dependencies and uses 100% native .oo source code.
It enforces zero ambient authority through 22 unforgeable capability tokens.
It provides microsecond execution across an Autonomic Reflex Stratum (tau <= 100 microseconds).
It scales across seven generational tiers from bare-metal silicon to distributed agent swarms.

```
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
|                           openOODA Standard Library Tiered Architecture                           |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
| Tier 4: Domain Applications (4,034 modules / 371,137 SLOC) - phys/, bio/, robot/, econ/, ai/, ui/ |
| Tier 3: Systems, I/O & Networking (1,085 modules / 102,408 SLOC) - net/, fs/, os/, io/, data/     |
| Tier 2: Security & Hardware (1,043 modules / 94,342 SLOC) - sec/, crypto/, hw/, simd/, compile/   |
| Tier 1: Universal Substrates (161 modules / 18,704 SLOC) - core/, sync/, collections/, principles |
+---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------+
```

